# The good FRU image with a single corrupted byte in the board info area, so
# the board area checksum no longer verifies. lib/ipmi_fru.c prints the fields
# anyway and reports "Board Area Checksum : INVALID"; a Zig port must keep
# doing exactly that rather than refusing the whole image.

@mark image
@fru/board.hex
@poke image 63 0xff   # board area checksum byte (area at 32, length 64)
